{"event_id": "evt_0011", "session": 1, "turn_no": 1, "world_time": "Sim, round 1", "actor": "gm", "kind": "gm_narration", "summary": "Narration for sbtest-001: Aero ignites, closes and disables the remote.", "visibility": "player", "knowledge_type": "fact", "known_to": [], "caused_by": ["evt_0005", "evt_0006", "evt_0007", "evt_0008", "evt_0009", "evt_0010"], "roll_ids": [], "tags": [], "details": {"text": "The holo-sim floor is bare and evenly lit, nothing between you and the training remote but fifteen feet of grey deck. It hangs at chest height, dead ahead, its emitter glowing that lazy orange. No cover, no other targets, the exit seam somewhere behind you.\n\n\"Again.\"\n\nYour thumb finds the slide on the hilt at your left hip. The indigo blade snaps out with a hiss and a low, steady hum that fills the quiet room, throwing violet-blue light across the deck plates.\n\nYou cover ten feet in two long strides. The remote is an arm's length away now, its little thrusters ticking as it begins to swing its emitter toward you.\n\nIt never finishes the turn. The blade comes across in one stroke and catches it clean across the casing (14 to hit; 10 energy damage). The shell parts with a bright crack and a smell of scorched plating. The orange glow gutters out. The remote drops, bounces once on the deck at your feet, and lies there smoking, its thrusters gone silent.\n\nA tinny voice, unhurried: *Remote disabled. Round complete.*\n\nThe only sounds left are the hum of your blade and the faint tick of cooling metal.\n"}, "idempotency_key": "sbtest-001:7"}
