{"event_id": "evt_0025", "session": 1, "turn_no": 2, "world_time": "Sim, after round 2", "actor": "gm", "kind": "gm_narration", "summary": "Narration for amw5ngpkju4m5k9: Aero walks over to the disabled remote.", "visibility": "player", "knowledge_type": "fact", "known_to": [], "caused_by": ["evt_0023", "evt_0024"], "roll_ids": [], "tags": [], "details": {"text": "You cross the deck toward it. Ten feet of grey plating, your boots loud on the metal in the quiet, the indigo blade still humming in your right hand and laying violet light across the floor ahead of you. The pistol hangs drawn in your left. Nothing moves anywhere in the sim room; the exit seam is behind you now, farther than before.\n\nYou stop with the remote five feet in front of you, close enough to reach in a single step. It sits where it fell on the deck, dark, still, the emitter dead. The scorched hole in its housing is right there, a thumb's width across, its edges blackened, the last thin thread of smoke still curling up out of it. The sharp ozone smell of the shot is stronger here.\n\nIt does not react to you. The room is silent except for the saber.\n"}, "idempotency_key": "amw5ngpkju4m5k9:3"}
