{"event_id": "evt_0035", "session": 1, "turn_no": 3, "world_time": "Sim, round 2", "actor": "gm", "kind": "gm_narration", "summary": "Narration for sbc2a01: 'Sim, hold the reset.'; the sim holds; Aero inspects the remote and cannot tell real burn from sim overlay by eye; hands full.", "visibility": "player", "knowledge_type": "fact", "known_to": [], "caused_by": ["evt_0030", "evt_0031", "evt_0032", "evt_0033"], "roll_ids": [], "tags": [], "details": {"text": "\"Sim, hold the reset.\"\n\nTwo flat notes from somewhere overhead. The room stays exactly as it is: grey deck plating, the exit seam far behind you, and the remote five feet in front of your boots, dark where it fell.\n\nYou look it over without touching it. The blade's light lays violet across the housing. The hole is a thumb's width across, the edges black, a thin thread of smoke still climbing out of it and bending in the room's slow air. It looks like a burn. It also looks like exactly what a training sim would draw on a target to tell you that you hit it. From here, with your eyes alone, you can't say which.\n\nThe saber hums in your right hand. The pistol hangs in your left, one shot spent. Nothing in the room moves.\n"}, "idempotency_key": "sbc2a01:8"}
